WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:04.750
2017 has already produced a ton of Hollywood
hits, like Disney's live-action version of

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:10.380
Beauty and the Beast, DC's long-awaited solo
pic for Wonder Woman, and Jordan Peele's sensational

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:11.990
breakout thriller Get Out.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.869
And it looks like the silver screen surprises
for this year aren't done just yet.

00:00:15.869 --> 00:00:19.800
Whether you're into action, comedy, horror,
or drama, there are plenty of forthcoming

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.960
films that'll be fighting for your movie ticket
money over the next several months.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.089
IT

00:00:25.089 --> 00:00:29.880
The 1990 TV miniseries adaptation of Stephen
King's IT amassed a cult following.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.649
But unfortunately, the four-hour feature's
laughable special effects and disorienting

00:00:33.649 --> 00:00:35.600
cutaways haven't aged well.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:40.739
Tim Curry's original performance as the town-terrorizing
clown Pennywise still set a high bar for anyone

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:42.280
to follow in the role, though.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:46.109
So, when the new version of the character,
played by Bill Skarsgård, was first revealed

00:00:46.109 --> 00:00:50.320
in a costume that could've easily been borrowed
from a schoolgirl's dress-up chest, it's only

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.970
natural that the movie faced a little blowback.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:56.969
But everything we've seen of IT since then
has been absolutely bone-chilling, and gives

00:00:56.969 --> 00:01:01.850
King fans reason to believe the new it-eration
will be floating atop the box office when

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:04.019
this movie lands on September 8th.

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:06.430
Kingsman: The Golden Circle

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:11.370
The creative team behind 2015's Kingsman:
The Secret Service reunites for this sequel,

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:15.320
which features the British spy team partnering
up with their American equivalents after their

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.350
headquarters are destroyed by a lethal foe.

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:18.450
"It's very American."

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:20.680
"Heh, yeah it is."

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:25.100
Original cast members like Taron Egerton and
Colin Firth are joined by an eclectic ensemble

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:29.380
that includes Channing Tatum, Halle Berry,
Julianne Moore, and Jeff Bridges for another

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:31.020
round of zany action.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.900
The Golden Circle hits theaters on September
22nd.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.320
"Time is running out."

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:37.320
Mother!

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:41.540
Director Darren Aronofsky has danced with
darkness in his films before, but with Mother!

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:44.090
he's going all-in on the horror genre at last.

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:48.110
The film features Jennifer Lawrence and Javier
Bardem as a couple who seem sublime — until

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:51.520
a bunch of unexpected house guests turn up
and all hell breaks loose.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.350
While the surreal trailer doesn't give much
away, we do know it'll feature bleeding walls

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:58.750
and mobs with torches — and Lawrence screaming
her heart out.

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:02.910
And with Aronofsky behind the lens, it's bound
to be creepy and emotionally disorienting.

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:05.860
September 15th can't get here soon enough.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:07.240
The LEGO Ninjago Movie

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:11.030
Yes, The LEGO Ninjago Movie is a feature-length
toy commercial.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:14.791
But its predecessors have managed to be pretty
swell, so we can probably expect some of the

00:02:14.791 --> 00:02:17.109
same animated awesomeness in this one, too.

00:02:17.109 --> 00:02:21.390
In the movie, Dave Franco's character Lloyd
sets off to stop his supervillain father Garmadon

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:25.340
and teams up with fellow ninjas and a master
martial artist, voiced by none other than

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:26.719
Jackie Chan himself.

00:02:26.719 --> 00:02:30.489
"I mean my mom is weird and collects seashells.

00:02:30.489 --> 00:02:34.010
Your dad levels cities and attacks innocent
people.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.850
So, they've all got their quirks you know?"

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:41.819
So get ready for another trip to LEGO land
this September 29th.

00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:42.819
American Made

00:02:42.819 --> 00:02:47.031
It's been a few decades since we last saw
Tom Cruise take the yoke of an airplane, but

00:02:47.031 --> 00:02:51.629
before he becomes Maverick again for Top Gun
2, this time he's hitting the air as a bored

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:55.890
commercial pilot who becomes one of the world's
most notorious drug smugglers.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:03:00.269
From the looks of it, when you're working
with the CIA, the DEA, and Pablo Escobar's

00:03:00.269 --> 00:03:04.310
drug cartel all at once, there's a pretty
good chance things will go sideways.

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:07.769
Count on this one to take flight on September
29th.

00:03:07.769 --> 00:03:09.120
Flatliners

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.790
If Flatliners sounds familiar, there's good
reason.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:16.250
This upcoming sci-fi thriller is actually
a sequel to a 1990 Kiefer Sutherland vehicle

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:17.349
of the same name.

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:21.469
Like the original, Flatliners features a group
of five medical students who undergo near-death

00:03:21.469 --> 00:03:24.900
experiences in an effort to document what
happens in the afterlife.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:28.849
When they return, they have brand new abilities
and insights — and might be going a little

00:03:28.849 --> 00:03:29.849
bit crazy.

00:03:29.849 --> 00:03:33.900
The new Flatliners comes across as more of
a traditional horror film than its predecessor,

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:38.010
but if it's half as eerie as it looks, it
should make the already-dense September 29th

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:41.189
release date slate even more competitive.

00:03:41.189 --> 00:03:43.370
Blade Runner 2049

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:47.760
Following up a towering sci-fi classic like
Blade Runner is a daunting task to the say

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.760
the least.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.519
But Blade Runner 2049 director Denis Villeneuve
has a few big things going for him.

00:03:52.519 --> 00:03:57.110
For one, Ridley Scott serves as producer on
the project, and Harrison Ford reprises his

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:58.630
role as Rick Deckard.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:03.310
Ford's also joined by an ensemble rounded
out by Ryan Gosling, Robin Wright, Jared Leto,

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:04.310
and Dave Bautista.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.639
"What do you want?"

00:04:05.639 --> 00:04:08.439
"I want to ask you some questions."

00:04:08.439 --> 00:04:11.999
Whether the end result can measure up to the
original remains to be seen, but if they can

00:04:11.999 --> 00:04:16.720
pull it off, Blade Runner 2049 could make
one helluva movie experience come October

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:17.720
6th.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:19.370
The Mountain Between Us

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:23.110
It's only a matter of time before Idris Elba
takes his rightful place as one of Hollywood's

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:27.130
top stars, and The Mountain Between Us might
be just the vehicle he needs.

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:31.130
In the film, he stars opposite Kate Winslet
in a landscape set amid hundreds of miles

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:35.620
of a barren, snowy wilderness, and the two
must team up to escape after surviving a plane

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:36.620
crash.

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:39.660
It might sound a little formulaic, but we
can probably count on these two powerhouses

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:44.150
to deliver some chilling performances when
this pic crashes into theaters on October

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.150
6th.

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:46.180
The Foreigner

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:50.630
This Jackie-Chan driven action flick features
the kung fu legend alongside Pierce Brosnan

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:53.430
reuniting with GoldenEye director Martin Campbell.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:57.250
The pic features Chan as the father of a young
woman who's killed in a terrorist attack,

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:59.150
launching him into revenge mode.

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:02.790
In the process, he runs afoul of Brosnan's
character, a British government official who

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:07.630
has ties to the IRA — and who might hold
the key to uncovering the attackers' identities.

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:11.250
Between Chan's killer training and Brosnan's
debonair style, The Foreigner should make

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:16.390
for one exhilarating game of cat and mouse
when it hits theaters October 13th.

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:17.820
Happy Death Day

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.941
It isn't Friday the 13th in America if there
isn't a schlocky horror film in theaters,

00:05:21.941 --> 00:05:23.960
and this year, it's Happy Death Day.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:27.590
It's basically Groundhog's Day meets Scream,
as the film features a college student who

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:31.870
has to relive the day of her death over and
over again until she figures out who's killing

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:32.870
her.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:36.410
If nothing else, it looks to be good for a
few fun jump scares and creative death scenes.

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:37.830
The Snowman

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:41.890
If campy horror isn't your preferred brand
of thrills, The Snowman might be what you're

00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:43.220
looking for instead.

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:47.310
The film follows a couple of detectives trying
to track down a serial killer who leaves icy

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:51.870
little clues to toy with his investigators
in a sleepy Swedish snowscape.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:56.280
With an all-star cast that includes Michael
Fassbender, Chloe Sevigny, and J.K. Simmons,

00:05:56.280 --> 00:06:00.650
we can expect The Snowman to be absolutely
bone-chilling once it hits theaters on October

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:01.810
20th.

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:03.900
Professor Marston &amp; the Wonder Women

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:07.750
If you haven't had enough of Wonder Woman
yet this year, give this origin story a try.

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:12.300
Professor Marston will give cinematic life
to the real-life man responsible for Diana

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.140
Prince, William Moulton Marston.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:18.090
And if you don't already know anything about
the author, let's just say he had some interesting

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:20.090
views on male-female relationships.

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:26.010
"A person is most happy when they are submissive
to a loving authority."

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:30.550
You'll learn all about it if you check out
this pic on October 27th.

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:31.620
Jigsaw

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:36.270
Lionsgate was definitely playing a game by
presenting 2010's Saw 3D: The Final Chapter

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:39.190
as the very last round of Jigsaw's punishing
plans.

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:43.560
In the newest round of torture trials, a copycat
killer appears to be reviving John Kramer's

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:47.750
work in ways that are a little too on the
nose for the investigators tailing this new

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:48.750
villain.

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:52.680
Just like the other pictures that preceded
it, Jigsaw looks to be chock full of psychological

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:57.000
and physical horrors that'll test your tolerance
for gore when this thing hits theaters on

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.300
October 27th.

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:00.300
Suburbicon

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:03.900
George Clooney and the Coen brothers have
already proven themselves to be an interesting

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:07.370
filmmaking match thanks to O Brother, Where
Art Thou? and Hail, Caesar!

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:10.780
And now the three have teamed up again — with
the Coens writing and Clooney directing — to

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:13.870
bring this quirky crime thriller to theaters
next.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:18.740
Suburbicon stars Matt Damon as a man who loses
his wife in a shocking home invasion incident

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:23.400
and watches as his idyllic little town turns
into a haven for deceit and darkness.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:27.150
As with any Clooney-Coen collaboration, this
grim landscape will be peppered with plenty

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:30.550
of comedy, making it a must-see on October
27th.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:35.060
Thor: Ragnarok
In Norse mythology, Ragnarök is an apocalyptic

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:39.110
series of events that results in the world
being plunged into water after the deaths

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:43.680
of several gods — including Odin, Thor,
and Loki — and culminates in a planetary

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:44.680
rebirth.

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:47.830
So, it's obvious from the title that this
chapter won't be a jolly good time for our

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:49.060
hammer-wielding hero.

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:50.190
"You have no idea."

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:54.420
The good news is, his imminent participation
in the upcoming Avengers: Infinity War means

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:57.590
he'll probably emerge from this adventure
relatively unscathed.

00:07:57.590 --> 00:08:01.070
But before that, he'll have to break out of
prison — without his hammer — and play

00:08:01.070 --> 00:08:03.980
gladiator opposite none other than The Incredible
Hulk.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:07.700
So, we can definitely count on this to be
a marvelous new adventure for our Avenger

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:10.680
friends when it busts into theaters on November
3rd.

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:13.380
"Surprise!

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.380
This is going to be such fun."

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:16.780
Daddy's Home 2

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:20.730
The first Daddy's Home didn't exactly thrill
critics, but audiences ate it up.

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:24.650
So, in true sequel fashion, Daddy's Home 2
is doubling down on everything that made the

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:29.050
first movie stand out — including twice
as many dads as the original.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:32.689
This time around, returning stars Will Ferrell
and Mark Wahlberg are joined by John Lithgow

00:08:32.689 --> 00:08:35.430
and Mel Gibson as their respective fathers.

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:39.969
Naturally, chaos ensues once this quartet
gets together, so prepare for some major dad

00:08:39.969 --> 00:08:44.279
jokes when this family comedy hits theaters
on November 10th.

00:08:44.279 --> 00:08:45.370
Justice League

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:49.660
As DC's biggest, boldest attempt at a shared
universe outing, Justice League will pull

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:55.050
together its all-star superhero squad of Wonder
Woman, Batman, Aquaman, The Flash, and Cyborg,

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:57.999
as they tangle with the latest villains to
threaten the Earth.

00:08:57.999 --> 00:09:01.980
If the massive receipts on Wonder Woman are
any indication, November 17th will be a big

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:06.550
day for the DC Extended Universe when this
superhero smash pic lands in theaters.

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:10.600
"They said the age of heroes would never come
again."

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:11.850
"It has to."

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:12.850
Coco

00:09:12.850 --> 00:09:17.509
As Pixar's first non-sequel since The Good
Dinosaur, Coco tells the story of a young

00:09:17.509 --> 00:09:20.399
boy named Miguel whose family has banned music.

00:09:20.399 --> 00:09:23.940
His love of instruments leads him to the Land
of the Dead, where he teams up with a trickster

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:27.980
named Hector to unravel his family's history
across both planes of existence.

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:33.529
Count on this Pixar pic to make a splash when
it bows into cinemas on November 22nd.

00:09:33.529 --> 00:09:35.300
The Disaster Artist

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:39.050
Tommy Wiseau's The Room is known for being
the single worst movie ever made, and James

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:43.820
Franco's The Disaster Artist aims to humorously
explore how such a terrible picture ever made

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:45.689
it to production in the first place.

00:09:45.689 --> 00:09:50.191
Unlike its source material, The Disaster Artist
is actually expected to be good, and will

00:09:50.191 --> 00:09:54.180
be a must-see for any movie fan when it lands
on December 8th.

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:55.509
The Shape of Water

00:09:55.509 --> 00:09:59.350
Guillermo del Toro has got a way with movie
monsters, and The Shape of Water looks to

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:01.370
be an especially beastly treat.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:05.930
The film stars Sally Hawkins, Michael Shannon
and Octavia Spencer, as it follows a disabled

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:10.449
janitor making pals with a water creature
that's tucked away in a secret research tank.

00:10:10.449 --> 00:10:14.959
With all the eerie atmosphere and authority
of del Toro's distinct eye behind this film,

00:10:14.959 --> 00:10:18.680
consider your calendar space for December
8th already booked.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:19.740
Ferdinand

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:24.279
In this animated pic, John Cena stars as the
pacifist animated bull Ferdinand, who must

00:10:24.279 --> 00:10:28.880
escape captivity to live his life of nonviolence
and merriment away from all the rodeos.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:33.420
The film is based on the classic children's
book by Munro Leaf and Robert Lawson.

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:37.089
Ferdinand will be a family favorite when it
drops just in time for holiday break from

00:10:37.089 --> 00:10:39.379
school on December 15th.

00:10:39.379 --> 00:10:41.670
Jumanji: Welcome to the Jungle

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:46.959
Welcome to the Jungle is expected to recapture
the magic of the 1995 adventure film Jumanji.

00:10:46.959 --> 00:10:51.750
But this time it features the Rock alongside
Jack Black, Karen Gillan, and Kevin Hart as

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:52.920
the players' avatars.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:56.660
And instead of rolling dice, the characters
will be playing a videogame that sucks its

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:58.190
heroes into a fictional jungle.

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:02.160
They'll have to fight their way to the exit
if they want to win … or at least live.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:04.200
"Damn that is a man right there."

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:08.240
"Don't cry, don't cry, don't cry, it's going
to be okay."

00:11:08.769 --> 00:11:10.360
Pitch Perfect 3

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:13.749
If you thought the first two Pitch Perfect
movies were awesome, you're in for a treat

00:11:13.749 --> 00:11:17.089
as the Bellas re-team for another round of
melodious shenanigans.

00:11:17.089 --> 00:11:20.750
This time, the Barden ladies will be performing
at a USO show, where they'll compete with

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:23.149
bands using real instruments for the first
time.

00:11:23.149 --> 00:11:27.920
So, prepare your pipes to sing right along
with your favorites when Pitch Perfect 3 harmonizes

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:31.149
with the holidays on its December 22nd release.

00:11:31.149 --> 00:11:33.559
"Let's aca-finish this."

00:11:33.559 --> 00:11:35.910
Star Wars: Episode VIII — The Last Jedi

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:40.079
After the success of The Force Awakens, the
new generation of Star Wars is coming back,

00:11:40.079 --> 00:11:44.999
with Daisy Ridley, John Boyega and Oscar Isaac
all returning to the big screen in this new

00:11:44.999 --> 00:11:45.999
chapter.

00:11:45.999 --> 00:11:49.259
But what we don't know is what will happen
to the rest of the originals, especially in

00:11:49.259 --> 00:11:53.449
the wake of Carrie Fisher's tragic and unexpected
death in 2016.

00:11:53.449 --> 00:11:57.870
The title of this installment seems to mean
that Luke Skywalker is the last of his kind,

00:11:57.870 --> 00:12:01.910
as the Resistance squares off against the
First Order, Snoke, and Kylo Ren.

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:06.649
Count on the box office force to be with Episode
8 when it hits theaters on December 15th.

00:12:06.649 --> 00:12:07.649
Thanks for watching!

00:12:07.649 --> 00:12:09.850
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:12.029
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

